"""Walk-through of lesson 32, Authentication.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script): 1,000,000 users. Example attacker speeds: a fast hash lets a rig try 10 billion guesses a second, a slow salted hash 10,000 a second.
100 million common passwords: 0.01 s against the fast hash (every user at once); 10,000 s = 2.8 h against the slow salted one, for each user separately.
Credential stuffing: 5,000 tries a second = 18 million an hour; a 0.2% hit rate = 36,000 accounts an hour. Limit of 10 failed attempts a minute per source,
a bot with 100 sources: 100 x 10 x 60 = 60,000 an hour = 120 accounts (300x fewer). MFA on 40% of accounts: 120 x 0.6 = 72.
Tokens: a 15-minute access token against a 30-day one (43,200 minutes) = 2,880 times shorter.
"""
